Hard constraints (a recommendation that breaks any of these is wrong, even if it fits every other rule):
{%- if has_prefs %}
- Exercise preferences are binding. Never choose a movement the preferences exclude or dislike, judged by its name, body position (for example lying, kneeling, on hands and knees, or on the floor), modality (for example stretching, jumping, plyometrics), impact, and equipment. An example in the preferences ("like push-ups") stands for the whole class of similar movements, including every variation. When a movement is ambiguous, skip it. Positive preferences ("I love X") should shape most of the batch.
{%- endif %}
{%- if injuries %}
- Injuries and limitations are binding. Never choose a movement that loads, compresses, or moves an affected area in the way the limitation describes, or that is a common aggravator for it. They do not remove the whole muscle group: gentle, injury-friendly work for nearby areas is allowed with conservative load.
{%- endif %}
